  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Work: No Child&apos;s Business - C&#xF4;te d&apos;Ivoire</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Accelerate progress to fight child labour in C&#xF4;te d&#x2019;Ivoire and strengthen child protection systems both through direct programmatic interventions and translating the area-based approach into national mechanisms and policies. The Alliance will focus on all four pillars of the broader ToC since their pertinence and complementarity applies also at country level. A phased approach to focus on the selected sectors has been selected in order to (i) drive momentum where best practices and engagement are already present (cocoa sector), and (ii) increase understanding and develop effective responses to sectors employing a sizeable number of children but that are less known (mining and domestic work).</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Work: No Child&#x2019;s Business&#x2019; is a programme of an alliance consisting of the Stop Child Labour Coalition, UNICEF Netherlands and Save the Children that aims to make a strong and lasting contribution to the elimination of child labour in C&#xF4;te d&apos;Ivoire.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">children &#x2013; victims or at risk of child labour - and their families</narrative>
  </description>
